cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "jev-vs-llm-tb-amr: catalog-grounded tuberculosis drug-resistance prediction with a System One decision model vs a generative LLM"
message: >-
  If you use this software or benchmark, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jiada
    family-names: Li
    email: jiadali2017@gmail.com
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-23"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jiadalee/jev-vs-llm-tb-amr"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible benchmark comparing two ways of answering the same 27 typed
  tuberculosis drug-resistance questions per isolate: Jev, a hosted System One
  decision model that returns calibrated typed answers in a single round trip,
  and a generative LLM (Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B) answering 27 sequential chat calls.
  Both arms judge identical, code-filtered evidence from a curated subset of
  the WHO 2021 M. tuberculosis resistance mutation catalogue, following the
  principle "filter first in code; judgment = model, facts = code". Across
  five isolates (97 decisions) the arms agree 95/97 (98%) while the decision
  model is 178-392x faster.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
